    "## Task 6: Propose a potential analytical solution (related to model or data) for mitigating the most severe limitation.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "97e3e8cd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The most severe limitation identified is the dataset’s overrepresentation of highly educated people and imbalance in gender, and the model’s bias towards the silent middle class. Because machine learning models like random forest optimize for overall accuracy, they naturally favor the dominant demographic groups and the most frequent class, ignoring underrepresented citizens.\n",
    "\n",
    "To mitigate this limitation without collecting new data, we can apply the idea of cost sensitive learning. In the paper of Chen et al. (2004), higher weights (panelties) are assigned to underrepresented demographic groups and minority classes, while the overrepresented group gets a lower weight assigned. By doing this we force the algorithm to pay more attention to these instances. \n"
   ]
